<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Coles Myer half yr net profit rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Coles Myer half yr net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>26 weeks to Jan 26</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net				     273.6 vs 194.5</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    341.3 vs 284.6</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     12.0 vs 12.0</p>
<p>    Abnormals		     profit 44.6 vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Coles Myer Ltd is Australia's largest retailer.  </p>
<p>NOTE: Business group performance (earnings before interest and tax)</p>
<p>    Supermarkets			  145.6 vs 128.7</p>
<p>    K Mart				   66.7 vs 50.6</p>
<p>    Target				   99.1 vs 86.1</p>
<p>    Fosseys			    loss 4.6 vs loss 4.2</p>
<p>    Myer/Grace Bros			83.1 vs 65.1</p>
<p>    Liquorland			     18.6 vs 15.3</p>
<p>    Red Rooster			     2.9 vs 4.2</p>
<p>    Katies				    4.9 vs 7.3</p>
<p>    Office Works		     loss 6.6 vs loss 4.5</p>
<p>    World 4 Kids		    loss 12.5 vs loss 20.1</p>
<p>    Property				 74.6 vs 49.7</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
